    <!--
        The app's icons: Lucide, under the ISC licence.

        Previously these were hand-authored path data, traced to match the
        design's own inline SVG. That was fine for the dozen the handoff drew
        and steadily worse for the ones it did not: a glyph nobody had drawn had
        to be invented, and an invented glyph is off-grid, off-weight and
        obvious beside a real one.

        Lucide is drawn on the same 24x24 grid with the round caps and joins the
        IconPath style already sets, so the set is consistent by construction
        rather than by eye.

        GENERATED. Do not hand-edit an entry: regenerate with
        desktop/tools/lucide_icons.py, which fetches the current SVGs and
        rewrites them as path data. Lucide draws with <circle>, <rect>, <line>
        and <polyline> as well as <path>, and a XAML Geometry takes only path
        mini-language — so a circle becomes two half-arcs, a rounded rect four
        lines and four arcs, and the rest straight M/L runs. The comment above
        each entry names the Lucide icon it came from.
    -->

